+// output into the SDPA's output_transpose_order. The micro SDPA kernel remaps the destination
+// strides from that order (convert_strides("DST", ...) in sdpa_gen_micro.cpp), so writing the
+// attention result out in the transposed layout is free there, whereas the standalone Transpose is
+// a full extra read+write of the [batch, heads, seq_len, head_size] tensor through a `permute_ref`
+// kernel. The canonical LLM/embedding attention block ends with exactly this
+// `SDPA -> Transpose(0, 2, 1, 3) -> Reshape -> o_proj` sequence.
